.TH SOCMOND 1 "October 2026" "OTA-Pulse" "OTA-Pulse Manual"
.SH NAME
socmond \- OTA-Pulse device monitoring daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B socmond
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects device metrics (CPU, memory, disk, network, temperature), captures crash dumps and the reason of the
last reboot, and uploads them to the backend. It is started by \fBsocmond.service\fR.
.PP
On the first start it registers with the provisioning token and stores the per-device API key in
\fI/var/lib/socmond/api_key\fR. The token is read from \fIauth.provisioning_token\fR in
\fI/etc/socmond/config.json\fR or, if that is empty, from \fI/etc/socmond/provisioning_token\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Use another configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/socmond/config.json
Configuration. Contains no credentials as shipped.
.TP
.I /etc/socmond/provisioning_token
Optional provisioning token (mode 0600).
.TP
.I /var/lib/socmond
Persistent state: API key, buffered metrics, core dumps.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soc-ctl (1),
.BR soc-deregister (1),
.BR socmond-watchdog (1),
.BR socmond-core-handler (1)
